# The web UI reads the xkb catalogue from xkb-data; without it the layout list
# falls back to a short built-in one, so the tool still works.
Recommends: xkb-data, libnotify-bin
Suggests: hyprland
Description: dynamic monitor configuration for Hyprland
 hyprdmc detects Hyprland outputs and positions, rotates, flips or mirrors
 them from a command line or a browser. A daemon watches for hotplug events
 and reapplies the profile matching the screens actually plugged in, with an
 automatic rollback when a change is not confirmed.
 .
 It also configures the keyboard layout and the pointer scroll direction,
 deliberately kept apart from the screen profiles: docking a laptop must not
 change what you type in.
